 "about_text": "Casa Ysasi is a studio and gallery in Los Angeles founded by brothers Iñigo and Pato Ysasi, built around a shared sense of hermandad, or brotherhood, rooted in family and craft. The space is divided between a gallery for exhibiting prints and curated work and a working studio and showroom where light-based objects and prototypes are developed. Ysasi Gallery operates as a rotating, two-month exhibition and installation platform, working with local and international artists whose practices sit between art, design, and craft, with an emphasis on process-driven, site-specific work. The studio side, Studio Ysasi, focuses on light as a medium, producing objects and installations meant to evoke presence and calm.",
